/*
 * Crop Sentinel AI — Phase 6: Zone tagging + history storage
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Scope (per §7 Phase 6): a zone-tag input screen (grid cell, e.g. "B4")
 * shown before each scan, and per-zone scan history stored in a fixed-size
 * in-memory ring buffer with timestamps.
 *
 * Acceptance test this file is built to satisfy: scan the same zone twice
 * and confirm both readings are retrievable and correctly ordered by time.
 * After every successful scan this sketch prints that zone's full stored
 * history to Serial (oldest -> newest) specifically so you can verify that
 * test by eye during the demo/dev loop.
 *
 * This file is Phase 5/6's sketch (TFT/touch bring-up, zone tagging,
 * history, JSON parsing) with the real Phase 4 TinyML model wired in,
 * replacing the earlier mean-threshold stub.
 *
 * ****** Phase 4 model ******
 * tinyModelVerdict() now runs the real fixed-point logistic regression
 * from tiny_model.h (generated by training/train_tiny_model.py). Make
 * sure tiny_model.h in this sketch folder is the one YOUR training run
 * produced, not the all-zero placeholder -- see the comment on that
 * function below.
 *
 * RAM DISCIPLINE (per §4.3): history is a small FIXED-size ring buffer,
 * not a growing list -- see MAX_ZONES / SCANS_PER_ZONE below. These were
 * tightened from (6,4,20) to (3,3,16) specifically to fix a real
 * "data section exceeds available space" compile error -- the original
 * values alone used ~840 bytes of this board's 2KB total RAM. The model
 * weights in tiny_model.h were also moved to PROGMEM (flash) for the same
 * reason, and the JSON reply parser was rewritten to stream field-by-field
 * instead of buffering a ~330+ byte line on the stack. If you hit RAM
 * trouble again, MAX_ZONES/SCANS_PER_ZONE/CLASS_NAME_LEN are still the
 * first things to shrink further.
 *
 * Libraries needed (Library Manager):
 *   - Adafruit GFX Library
 *   - Adafruit ILI9341
 *   - XPT2046_Touchscreen (Paul Stoffregen)
 */

